\title{The exterior shadow of a Clifford algebra}

\p{The Clifford relation lowers word length by two. Filtering by word length therefore separates a word from its contraction terms: the highest-degree part is alternating, and the associated graded algebra is the exterior algebra. Reversal then distinguishes word order from parity, while orthogonality gives a scalar square for a volume word.}

